**The open front — a critical, reproducible on-disk corruption (Defect A):** under an 8-node create storm, peer nodes write **stale cached dir-block images while holding only PR (19 captured) or after release (1, via xfsaild)**; interleaved with the real holder's leaf→node split write, they tear the block on the LUN → CRC failure → 5-of-8-node shutdown cascade. Root proven with per-write granted-mode tracing; reproduces on a fresh filesystem in ~30s. A GPT design review produced the fix blueprint (tenure-authorized write fence + exhaustive publish registry); the provably-safe v1 fence is specced with exact code sites in state.md and ccmemory for the next session. Defect B (dir format-decision TOCTOU, EUCLEAN-only) is the same family read-side.

